The UEP should be implemented as a middleware layer with the following components:

1. Message passing system with standardized JSON schema
2. Task state management (pending, in-progress, completed, failed)
3. Context sharing mechanism for passing data between agents
4. Event logging and tracing for observability
5. Retry and fallback logic for resilience

Implementation should use an event-driven architecture with:
- Message queue for asynchronous communication
- WebSocket or similar for real-time updates
- Serialization/deserialization of agent contexts
- Timeout handling to meet <1s latency requirement

Pseudo-code:
```javascript
class UEP {
  constructor() {
    this.messageQueue = new MessageQueue();
    this.contextStore = new SharedContextStore();
    this.eventLogger = new EventLogger();
  }

  async sendMessage(fromAgent, toAgent, payload, options = {}) {
    const message = {
      id: generateUUID(),
      timestamp: Date.now(),
      from: fromAgent,
      to: toAgent,
      payload,
      options
    };

    this.eventLogger.log('message.sent', message);
    await this.messageQueue.publish(message);
    return message.id;
  }

  async subscribeToMessages(agentId, callback) {
    return this.messageQueue.subscribe(agentId, callback);
  }

  async shareContext(contextId, data, accessControl = []) {
    return this.contextStore.set(contextId, data, accessControl);
  }

  async getContext(contextId, requestingAgent) {
    return this.contextStore.get(contextId, requestingAgent);
  }
}
```

