The Shared Context Layer should be implemented as a centralized service that:

1. Stores and retrieves context data for all agents
2. Manages access control for sensitive information
3. Handles versioning of shared contexts
4. Provides real-time updates when context changes
5. Supports structured and unstructured data

Implementation details:
- Use a distributed key-value store for persistence
- Implement pub/sub for real-time updates
- Create access control mechanisms
- Support JSON schema validation for structured data
- Include versioning and history tracking

Pseudo-code:
```javascript
class SharedContextLayer {
  constructor() {
    this.store = new DistributedKeyValueStore();
    this.pubsub = new PubSubSystem();
    this.accessControl = new AccessControlManager();
    this.schemaValidator = new JsonSchemaValidator();
  }

  async set(contextId, data, metadata = {}, accessControl = []) {
    const timestamp = Date.now();
    const version = await this.getNextVersion(contextId);

    const contextEntry = {
      id: contextId,
      data,
      metadata: {
        ...metadata,
        timestamp,
        version
      },
      accessControl
    };

    if (metadata.schema) {
      this.schemaValidator.validate(data, metadata.schema);
    }

    await this.store.set(this.getKey(contextId, version), contextEntry);
    await this.pubsub.publish(`context.${contextId}.updated`, contextEntry);

    return { contextId, version };
  }

  async get(contextId, version = 'latest', requestingAgent) {
    const key = version === 'latest' 
      ? await this.getLatestVersionKey(contextId)
      : this.getKey(contextId, version);

    const contextEntry = await this.store.get(key);

    if (!contextEntry) {
      throw new Error(`Context not found: ${contextId} (version: ${version})`);
    }

    if (!this.accessControl.canAccess(requestingAgent, contextEntry)) {
      throw new Error(`Access denied: ${requestingAgent} cannot access ${contextId}`);
    }

    return contextEntry;
  }

  async subscribe(contextId, callback) {
    return this.pubsub.subscribe(`context.${contextId}.updated`, callback);
  }

  // Helper methods...
}
```

